# Agentic-surface nginx routing — apply to /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/tilla.gudman.xyz.conf
#
# Problem this fixes: the app registers a root MCP concierge (app/agentic.py:1697
# POST /mcp, :1712 GET /mcp — advertised in the live agent card's discovery block),
# per-store MPP channel ops (app/mpp.py: /s/{slug}/mpp/open|voucher|topup|close),
# subscriptions (app/subscriptions.py: /s/{slug}/subscribe[/prepare|/encode|
# /cancel/prepare|/cancel]), B2B wholesale quotes (app/agentic.py:1775
# GET /s/{slug}/quote) and verified-buyer reviews (app/agentic.py:1839
# GET /s/{slug}/reviews) — but nginx had no locations for any of them, so every
# one of these answered the static-site 404 while the rails behind them were
# enabled (and in several cases already settled real value on-chain, see
# docs/PROOF-onchain.md). The "four x402 schemes" surface existed only on
# 127.0.0.1:8040.
#
# Two changes:
#
# 1) Root MCP concierge — add at the server{} (443) level:
#
#     location = /mcp { proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8040; proxy_set_header Host $host; proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr; proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for; proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https; }
#
# 2) Widen the per-store agent-surface regex. Replace:
#
#     location ~ ^/s/[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]+/(buy(/[0-9]+)?|mcp|feed\.json|llms\.txt|feed/openai\.json|feed/google\.xml)$ {
#
#    with:
#
#     location ~ ^/s/[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]+/(buy(/[0-9]+)?|mcp|reviews|quote|feed\.json|llms\.txt|feed/openai\.json|feed/google\.xml|mpp/(open|voucher|topup|close)|subscribe(/prepare|/encode|/cancel/prepare|/cancel)?)$ {
#
#    (body of the block unchanged — same proxy_pass + headers as before).
#
# Application procedure (same discipline as every nginx change):
#   1. cp the live conf to /opt/tilla/nginx-backups/tilla.conf.pre-agentic
#   2. Edit the two lines above.
#   3. nginx -t   — MUST pass before any reload.
#   4. systemctl reload nginx
#   5. Verify from outside: POST https://tilla.gudman.xyz/mcp returns JSON (not the
#      HTML 404 page); GET /s/invoice-flow/quote answers JSON; POST
#      /s/invoice-flow/mpp/open and /s/invoice-flow/subscribe answer app JSON
#      (402/4xx from the app, never text/html); GET /s/invoice-flow/reviews → 200.
#
# Dormancy note: exposing these locations does NOT enable anything — every rail
# keeps its own flag/creds gating in the app. nginx exposure only makes the
# already-enabled surfaces answer the same way they do on localhost.
